  {
   "topic": "Output enable",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "G is active LOW. While G is LOW the output Y drives the level on A; while G is HIGH, Y is high-impedance whatever A is."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Overvoltage tolerance",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The inputs tolerate 5.5 V, and the output has 5.5 V power-down protection: with VCC = 0 V or the output disabled, VOUT may sit anywhere from 0 V to 5.5 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Unused inputs",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "An input that is not used is tied to VCC or to GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Timing measurement",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Propagation delays are taken with the switch open. Enable and disable times to and from the LOW level (tPZL, tPLZ) use the switch at twice VCC; those to and from the HIGH level (tPZH, tPHZ) use it at GND."
  }
